-
-Backport of vLLM PR #52816 ("[Spec Decode] DFlash2: local convolution + candidate
-selector", SubSir, Aug 2026) onto 0.27.1, plus the pieces of vLLM main it silently relies
-on and what our stack needs:
-  - PR: DFlash2DraftModel (model_executor/models/qwen3_dflash2.py: grouped dynamic
-    convolutions + candidate selector), the V2-runner DFlash2Speculator
-    (v1/worker/gpu/spec_decode/dflash2/), registry + use_v2_model_runner hooks,
-    is_causal precedence in _dflash_layer_causal (the DFlash2 config is top-level
-    is_causal=false with all-sliding layer_types; without this hunk the drafter runs
-    causal).
-  - main: sample_idx_mapping sentinel -1 (DFlash2's kernels test req_state >= 0;
-    with 0.27.1's zero-init the CUDA-graph capture would scatter every padding row into
-    request slot 0 and poison its proposal distribution); DFlash prepare-inputs kernel
-    hardening (rejected-suffix context rows and null-block entries of a sliding-window
-    block table no longer write draft KV into physical block 0; seq_lens clamp);
-    DFlash reserves K draft slots per request (not K-1); NaN guards before the
-    rejection sampler's argmax.
-  - 0.27.1 caches temperature-APPLIED draft logits (main caches pre-temperature and
-    divides on load), so the selector walk stores scores/temperature — without this the
-    lossless verify would use softmax(scores) while the draft sampled from
-    softmax(scores/T) for 0 < T != 1.
-  - our stack: the draft shares the target's int8-Marlin lm_head, so compute_candidates
-    accepts any quant_method with apply() (2-D input); the context-KV precompute
-    dequantizes k/v rows from a W4A16 (compressed-tensors) qkv_proj so the drafter itself
-    can be requantized (prepare/fetch_dflash2.py / drafter/quant_dflash2.py); flashinfer.top_k
-    falls back to torch.topk if its JIT build fails (VLLM_DFLASH2_TORCH_TOPK=1 forces
-    torch.topk); the V2 sampler passes k_max so patches/sampler-small-topk-fast-softmax's
-    sort-free small-k top-k/top-p path is used under the V2 runner too; the selector
-    walk applies the request's top-k/top-p to its 16-candidate proposal and caches the
-    truncated q (the DFlash2 analogue of the MTP draft truncation; lossless;
-    VLLM_DFLASH2_DRAFT_TOPK_TOPP=0 disables), with the model runner handing the
-    sampling-state buffers to the speculator.
