-int8-QK Triton prefill attention for the head_dim-256 full-attention layers.
-
-FA2's hd256 prefill runs at 54-57 TFLOPS on a 250 W RTX 3090 — about 85% of
-the card's practical fp16 tensor-core rate — so no fp16 rewrite can win. This
-kernel runs the QK^T GEMM on int8 tensor cores (2x the fp16 mma rate),
-SageAttention-style, and keeps P.V in bf16:
-
-  - K is smoothed by its per-(head, channel) mean over the context before
-    quantization. For a fixed query row q, q . mean_k is identical for every
-    key, so the softmax is invariant to the subtraction and the correction
-    term is never computed. Exactness survives up to int8 rounding.
-  - K is gathered from the paged cache, mean-smoothed and absmax-quantized
-    ONCE per layer-chunk into contiguous int8 scratch (per 64-key, per-head
-    scales); the hot loop loads int8 K with no page gather and no quant work.
-  - Q rows carry per-row absmax scales, quantized in-kernel.
-  - Output accuracy: cos > 0.99999 against an fp32 reference at kv 4k-51k
-    (FA2 itself measures 0.999997); end-to-end PPL/GSM8K gated before ship.
-
-Measured on the serving shapes (24 q-heads / 4 kv-heads, D=256, causal,
-2048-token chunk, paged bf16 KV, block 16), min-of-rounds:
-
-  kv=4096   FA2 2.72 ms   this 2.14 ms   1.27x
-  kv=16384  FA2 14.22 ms  this 10.91 ms  1.30x
-  kv=51200  FA2 47.07 ms  this 34.91 ms  1.35x
-
-In serving (single-user dflash2 stack, int8-GEMM config) it is worth +0.4%
-at 1k rising to +5.3% at 51k end-to-end prefill, because a chunked 51k
-prefill spends ~28% of its time in attention at the average context depth.
-
-VLLM_PREFILL_ATTN=int8 turns it on (fp16 selects the scaffold mode, off/unset
-keeps FA2). The branch fires only for single-request prefill chunks
-(max_seqlen_q > 16, one request in the varlen batch) on the exact serving
-geometry, with bf16 KV, causal, and no window/softcap/alibi/sinks — anything
-else falls through to FA2. Decode and the split-KV verify path are untouched.
-
-Apply from the installed vllm package directory, AFTER spec-decode-attn.patch:
-its flash_attn.py hunk inserts immediately before that patch's split-KV block
-and carries that block's first lines as context, so the file name sorts after
-spec-decode-*.patch on purpose -- the Docker gate and verify.sh apply
-patches/*.patch alphabetically (this is why it was named triton-... and not
-prefill-...: CI was red for four commits with 'Hunk #1 FAILED at 1038').
-  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/triton-prefill-attn-int8.patch
-
-Written against vLLM 0.27.1.
